# Frontend conventions (Planning.Web)

- API access goes through the **orval-generated client** (`app/generated/**`) wrapped by
  a `composables/api/use*Api.ts` composable, combined with TanStack Vue Query
  (`composables/queries/*`) for server state. This is the target pattern for new code.
- `utils/planningClient.ts` is a legacy hand-written client with manual
  PascalCase/camelCase normalization (`normalizeRecord`). That dual-casing symptom means
  the API contract is out of sync — don't copy this pattern into new modules. Prefer
  migrating toward the generated client over extending the manual normalizer.
- TypeScript `strict: true`; ESLint enforces `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any: 'error'`.
  Don't use `any`/`as any` to route around a type error — fix the type.
- Respect the existing ESLint config instead of reformatting around it: tabs for Vue
  template indentation, single quotes, always-multiline trailing commas, one attribute
  per line in templates, no `console.log` (only `info`/`warn`/`error` allowed).
- Auth/session state lives in `stores/auth.ts` (Pinia), tokens in `useCookie`
  (`planning_access_token`, `planning_refresh_token`, `planning_organization_id`). Route
  gating lives in `middleware/*.global.ts`. Don't add a second, parallel auth-state
  mechanism (e.g. localStorage) — extend the store.
- Client-side validation (`app/schemas/*`) is UX only, never the security boundary — the
  server-side FluentValidation validator is authoritative.

## XSS is critical here, not routine

Access/refresh tokens live in a JS-readable cookie (`useCookie`, not httpOnly) — any XSS
is a full account takeover, not just a defacement. Treat unsanitized rendering of
user-provided content (`v-html`, `innerHTML`, dynamically built URLs, `eval`) as high
severity. Prefer plain interpolation; if `v-html` is ever unavoidable, sanitize first and
call it out explicitly rather than leaving it implicit.
